ses my  config stayed silent even when you're  maxing out the CP using Cinebench and  the GPU with Unigine heaven at the same  time there are just three fans for  general cooling with no direct fans on  the graphics cards and they literally  stayed right around idle is a gaming  both with the LG 5k and also when we  finally got the super backordered  6kx dr and the vega to graphics card  performed better than we expected in  boot camp getting right around that  coveted consistent 60 FPS out ultra  settings in forza and that's at 5k  resolution which is pushing 15 million  pixels instead of 8 million in 4k we  also play call of duty at 6k resolution  which is over 20 million pixels and got  50 to 60 frames per second at medium  settings and trust us  6k at medium settings looks a fair bit  better than 4k at Ultra editing video  was also really amazing on this Mac I do  video production outside of YouTube and  we mostly work in Final Cut for speed  reasons so owning a Mac is required yes  there are hacking Tosh's which i've  actually built many of myself and i'm  gonna be doing another one soon using  thread Ripper to pit against this Mac  Pro but for daily professional work and  legal reasons I definitely prefer a true  Mac I connected to Mac Pro to our 112  tear by q-not with 10 Gigabit Ethernet  for video editing which works perfectly  out closer to a thousand megabytes a  second and since the Mac Pro has two of  these ports I ordered a new network hard  for our server and I'm excited to test  out link aggregation to get close to two  thousand megabytes per second so if  everything seems so good what is the  hesitation or regret well no it's not  the price even though it is very  expensive but for a well-functioning  business with employees a fifteen  thousand dollar computer that will last  many years is nothing compared to all  the other costs involved like taxes  insurance brand payroll benefits and  much much more  my issue is how much of this system is  being 