e MacBook Pro can  render a graded five-minute 4k raw 60fps  project in 10 minutes and 50 seconds  using Final Cut and if you're using my  much more powerful Mac Pro with premiere  it takes 25 minutes now rendering isn't  everything but even if you're editing in  a timeline this MacBook will playback  over 50 frames per second a full quality  whereas the Mac Pro and premier can only  do that at 24 frames per second because  of its inefficiency and to get better  results you would want a better  processor either maybe a 16 core or  higher this really shows how important  it is not only to have good Hardware but  it's even more important to have new  modern software that can make the best  use of it this is where my regrets start  coming in the new faster MacBook pairs  on my software that is so crazy  efficient means that I no longer need  hardware as powerful as a Mac Pro's in  order to have a fantastic video editing  experience like I did six months ago of  course there are still people who will  need more power but thanks to Apple that  market is now smaller now I mention that  there is one specific reason why I don't  regret getting a Mac Pro and that's  because we make videos like this one  where we don't earn any money on the  production but by having the hardware to  test  and make videos on not only do we earn  income but we also get to provide  knowledge and entertainment as well as  save a lot of people money with our  tests our comparisons our reviews and  also provide good suggestions to help  people get their right gear which makes  our Mac Pro purchase well worth it if it  wasn't for that I would regret buying  this aluminum beast not because it's not  good enough but thanks to Apple in their  new software it is too good for me and a  lot of other people where it wasn't just  six months ago I also mentioned  long-term meditations with this Mac Pro  for myself and others and that's because  there is a lack of PCI Express 4 and  also the CPU socket that's in here Apple  has been using Intel for many years now  and in the past four years they've  really been limited by Intel's constant  delays of 10 nanometer chips where AMD  is now serving amazing 7 nanometer  threat or adversity views I really hope  that Apple changes over to AMD or at  least offers an AMD Mac Pro but for now  it's just Intel which doesn't support  PCI Express 4 and also switches CPU  sockets much more frequently meaning  that future CPUs that come out may not  be supported in this computer now that  will mean big price drops on these  currency pews and those that want to  upgrade to a higher core count later  will be you know be able to do that much  cheaper but with the way software is  going if you're a Video Editor you don't  really need more powerful CPUs so there  you guys have it do I regret the Mac Pro  well no because on a business level  makes a whole lot of sense for us and  for those doing other kinds of work that  needs high end hardware with Mac OS it  makes sense as well because it's  actually cheaper than buying a high-end  iMac Pro and you get more power and more  ports and you also get upgrade ability  go ahead and let me know your thoughts  down in the comment section below and  check out our links in the video  description for the other kind of videos  and topics I talked about click up there  to subscribe and if you want to see some  other great videos there are a few right  over there  this Ben Max and I will see you in the  next video  [Music]

